Package: AnnR
Type: Package
Title: Fast and Faithful 'AnnData' ('.h5ad') Input/Output for R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Md Babu", "Mia", email = "md.babu.mia@mssm.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Reads and writes 'AnnData' '.h5ad' files (the on-disk format of the
    Python 'anndata' package) directly from R through a native C++ engine linked
    against the 'HDF5' C library. Chunks are fetched and decompressed in
    parallel (gzip via 'libdeflate' or 'zlib', LZF, Zstandard) and decoded
    straight into R memory, sparse matrices are mapped onto 'Matrix' classes
    without copies, and every 'anndata' encoding (including legacy files written
    by 'anndata' < 0.7) is supported. Original on-disk data types are recorded
    so that files written back from R reproduce the source dtypes and encodings.
    Converters to and from 'SingleCellExperiment' and 'Seurat' objects are
    included.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    Matrix (>= 1.6-0),
    methods,
    parallel,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    BiocGenerics,
    DelayedArray,
    jsonlite,
    S4Vectors,
    SeuratObject (>= 5.0.0),
    SingleCellExperiment,
    SummarizedExperiment,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
LinkingTo:
    cpp11
SystemRequirements: C++17, HDF5 C library (>= 1.10.5), zlib; optionally
    libdeflate and libzstd for faster decompression
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
